   "paragraph": "Arm can earn money from the same chip design in two ways. A company pays a license fee to use the design, then pays Arm a royalty when it ships chips based on that design. Think of paying for access to a blueprint, then paying a fee for each product built from it. Arm reported quarterly revenue of $1.44 billion, up 27% from a year earlier, and said its data centre royalties doubled. It also plans to sell its own Arm AGI CPU, the main processor in a computer. Arm estimates up to $2 billion in sales from that chip over two fiscal years, depending on demand and supply.",
